From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:25:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give ExtensionLoadOptions a constructor from the extension name

ExtensionLoadOptions is an aggregate of the extension name and an
alias, and every caller that loads an extension by name builds it with
a braced list of the name alone, so -Wmissing-field-initializers
reports the alias at each of those seven call sites. A constructor
from the name, with the default constructor kept for the callers that
set the members one by one, takes the braced lists as before and
leaves the alias default-initialized, which is what the aggregate did;
it is the shape upstream gives the struct later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_load_options.hpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_load_options.hpp b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_load_options.hpp
index efc87e8da8..c0a9f1ae72 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_load_options.hpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/extension_load_options.hpp
@@ -14,6 +14,11 @@
 namespace duckdb {
 
 struct ExtensionLoadOptions {
+	ExtensionLoadOptions() = default;
+	// NOLINTNEXTLINE: allow implicit conversion from the extension name
+	ExtensionLoadOptions(string extension_name) : extension_name(std::move(extension_name)) {
+	}
+
 	string extension_name;
 	Identifier alias;
 };
